## Intuition
To find the median of the matrix, we can first store all the elements into a single vector.
Once all elements are in one place, sorting them will arrange them in increasing order.
Since median is the middle element of the sorted list, we can directly return it.

## Approach
Create an empty vector arr.
Traverse each row and each element of the matrix.
Push every element into arr.
Sort the vector.
Find the middle index using arr.size()/2.
Return the element at that index.

## Solution
//code here
class Solution {
public:
    int median(vector<vector<int>> &mat) {
        vector<int> arr;

        for(auto row : mat) {
            for(auto x : row) {
                arr.push_back(x);
            }
        }

        sort(arr.begin(), arr.end());

        return arr[arr.size()/2];
    }
};

